-- title:
--   Transfer of level automorphisms to the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $A_0$ denotes the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ of $k_0$, i.e. `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`.
--
--   **Arithmetic parameters.** A prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a natural number $\ell_g$ which is prime (`hℓg`), satisfies $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓg12`), divides $M'$ (`hℓgM'`) and lies in `M'.primeFactors` (`hℓgpf`).
--
--   **The place above $q$ and its reduction data.** A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. the rational affine geometric places $w$ with $w$-value of the geometric $j$-generator lying in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)` (`hW`); the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the base change of the $\mathbb{Q}$-function field of level $q^2M'$ and subgroup `levelH q M'` (`hle`); a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` relative to $A$, that is, a valuation subring of integers whose residue map onto the target is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal, restricting to the residue map of $A$ on constants, with the scaling property that every non-zero function has a non-zero residue after multiplication by a constant, and with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of functions; finally the hypothesis `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Local data over $k_0$.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), such that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is Henselian local (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Root of unity, level and function field.** An element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`) and admits a ring embedding $k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ sending it to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$ (`hιξ`); the subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ equal to the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$ (`hH₁`), so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$; the intermediate field $K$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$ obtained as the base change `laurentBaseChange` to $k_0$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁` of level $q^2M'$ and subgroup $H_1$ (`hK`), with the algebra and scalar-tower structures of $A_0$ on $K$ through $k_0$; and an element $j \in K$, non-zero, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image in $k_0$ of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant (`hj`).
--
--   **Functoriality of level structures.** The hypothesis `hℓ`: for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every level-$p$ datum $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$, if $D$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $W$ — that is, $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation, $x_P$ is a root of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}$, and $(x_Q,y_Q) = (x_P,y_P)$ — then the transformed datum `D.variableChange C` is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $C \bullet W$. The hypothesis `hM`: likewise `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (which for $p^k = 2$ is the two-torsion kernel condition on $h$ and otherwise the cyclic generator kernel condition) is preserved when $W$ is replaced by $C \bullet W$ and $h$ by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`.
--
--   **The Drinfeld level package over $A_0$.** A family of group laws $\mathcal{G}$ on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`, each group law admits a points-evaluation identification with affine points which is additive and Galois-equivariant) and with identity section the origin chart section killing $x/y$ and $z/y$ (`h𝒢O`); a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ of raw Drinfeld pairs of level $q$ for $\mathcal{G}$, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`: its variable-change and coefficient-change actions carry the two sections to the expected ones through the graded homomorphisms of the Proj coordinate rings); the hypothesis `hVC`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every projective Weierstrass curve and every variable change $C$ there is a graded ring homomorphism between the Proj coordinate rings realising $C$ in the sense of `IsVariableChangeHom`, subject to the containment of irrelevant ideals needed to induce a morphism of Proj; and `hCO`, the analogous statement for coefficient homomorphisms along an $A_0$-algebra map $f$, realising $f$ in the sense of `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   **The cyclotomic frame.** A field $L_1$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{q\ell_g\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta_1$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ₁`), $\xi_1$ a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity (`hξ₁`) and $\zeta_1 = \xi_1^{\ell_g}$ (`hζξ₁`); the intermediate field $K_1$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L_1)/L_1$ obtained from the same $\mathbb{Q}$-function field by base change to $L_1$ (`hK₁`); a discrete valuation ring $A_1$ with fraction field $L_1$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal (`hA₁q`) and $\zeta_1$ in the image of $A_1$ (`hζA₁`), acting on $K_1$ compatibly through $L_1$; a non-zero $j_1 \in K_1$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of `jq` in $L_1$ (`hj₁`); a uniformiser $\varpi_1$ of $A_1$ (`hϖ₁`); a point $z_1$ of the two-chart integral model `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ ↥K₁ j₁` together with the element $\varpi_{z_1}$ of its stalk at $z_1$ obtained as the germ at $z_1$ of the global section pulled back from $\varpi_1$ along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ (`hϖz₁`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz₁`), so that $z_1$ lies in the special fibre; a point $y_1$ of the affine chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A₁ ↥K₁ j₁` mapping to $z_1$ (`hy₁`); and `hss₁`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A₁ ↥K₁ j₁` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y_1$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with this $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The comparison embedding.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : L_1 \to k_0$ with $\iota(\zeta_1) = \xi$ (`hιζ₁`), carrying $A_1$ into $A$ (`hιA`), and such that any $x \in L_1$ with $\iota(x) \in A$ already comes from $A_1$ (`hιA'`).
--
--   Here `chartAlgFin R F j` denotes the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over $R[j]$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $L_1$-algebra automorphism $\tau_1$ of $K_1$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L₁ q ζ₁ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K₁ τ₁` — the $q$-expansion condition that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ having non-zero associated Laurent series, every $x \in K_1$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of the series of $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every embedding of $L_1$ into $\mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta_1$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the image of $\tau_1 x$ under that embedding times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ — and every proof $\mathrm{hpres}_1$ that $\tau_1$ maps `chartAlgFin A₁ ↥K₁ j₁` into itself, there exist
--
--   1. a ring homomorphism $c$ from `chartAlgFin A₁ ↥K₁ j₁` to `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K j`,
--
--   2. a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$,
--
--   3. a proof that `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` holds, the same $q$-expansion condition over $k_0$ with $\xi$ in place of $\zeta_1$,
--
--   4. a proof $\mathrm{hpres}$ that $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K j` into itself,
--
--   such that both of the following hold: first, for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A₁ ↥K₁ j₁`, the Laurent series over $k_0$ attached to $c(a)$ is the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of the Laurent series over $L_1$ attached to $a$; second, the restriction of the underlying ring homomorphism of $\tau$ to `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K j` (using $\mathrm{hpres}$) composed after $c$ equals $c$ composed after the restriction of the underlying ring homomorphism of $\tau_1$ to `chartAlgFin A₁ ↥K₁ j₁` (using $\mathrm{hpres}_1$).
--
--   This is the transfer step, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-guarded ("diamond") frame, which moves a level automorphism of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ from the cyclotomic model over $L_1$, with its discrete valuation ring $A_1$, to the model over the subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ determined by the chosen place $A$ above $q$, simultaneously producing the coefficientwise comparison map of integral $j$-charts and the commutation of the two restricted automorphisms. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_ringHom_chartAlgFin_levelAut_comap_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_ringHom_cyclotomic_rigidDataGamma1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_ringHom_chartAlgFin_levelAut_comap_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_ringHom_cyclotomic_rigidDataGamma1Pow) in the construction of the supersingular specialisation of the modular curve that underlies the level-lowering argument.
